    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The two pillars of Italian",
     "texto": [
      "**Essere** and **avere** are essential, irregular auxiliary verbs. It's worth learning their six present forms by heart.",
      "In **avere**, the forms **ho**, **hai**, **ha** and **hanno** have a compulsory silent **h** in writing: it stops them being confused in writing with **o** (or), **ai** (to the, plural), **a** (to) and **anno** (year). In pronunciation, the «h» is never pronounced."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
